; Project npm configuration
;
; react-scripts@5.0.1 declares an outdated optional peer dependency on
; typescript "^3.2.1 || ^4", but this project deliberately uses TypeScript 5.x
; (typescript ^5.3.0, resolved 5.9.3). react-scripts 5 is fully compatible with
; TypeScript 5 in practice; only the published peer range is stale.
;
; Under npm v7+ (here npm 11) strict peer-dependency resolution rejects this
; combination, causing `npm ci` / `npm install` to fail with ERESOLVE. The
; package-lock.json was generated with legacy peer handling and already pins the
; full, working dependency graph (typescript 5.9.3 + react-scripts 5.0.1).
;
; Enabling legacy-peer-deps restores the npm v6 behavior of ignoring peer
; conflicts during resolution, allowing deterministic installs from the lock
; file without modifying any source code.
legacy-peer-deps=true
